From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u, winex11, user32, explorer: each monitor has its own scale, as on Windows

LogPixels was every monitor's scale, and the automatic scale follows the main
display: with a 1440p main display at 125% beside a 1080p one, the 1080p one
was 125% too, and unplugging the 1440p one turned every window from 125% to
100% and back (GitHub report, ledger i0621). Now each monitor keeps its own:
HKCU\Control Panel\Desktop\PerMonitorSettings\<monitor>\DpiValue, steps from
its recommended scale in Windows' list, as Windows keeps it; without one the
recommended scale for its size (the session's rule). A scale picked for all
monitors before (no settings of each monitor's) stays every monitor's.
The monitor is named by its EDID, which Xwayland does not give: winex11 reads
it from the kernel's connector. A window moved onto a monitor of another scale
is told (WM_DPICHANGED) or scaled by Wine; DisplayConfigGetDeviceInfo and
DisplayConfigSetDeviceInfo read and set a display's scale with Windows' types
(-3, -4); the other displays' taskbars are drawn at their display's scale; a
monitor unplugged while the displays are read no longer ends the programs
reading them (Xlib's handler on BadRROutput).
